; Shed for a void, and the setter's throwaways. Winning 42 pp. 43-48
; (S-0064-c, S-0064-d, S-0065-b, S-0065-c, S-0070-d), p. 49 (S-0071-a,
; S-0071-b; S-0072-a, the first and third of the five key points: hold
; doubles and count, create voids) and p. 79 (S-0108-a); played in Hands 32 and 33 (S-0142-g,
; S-0144-d), and foreseen in Hand 12 (S-0044-a). The throwaways: the worked
; deals, Hands 28 to 33 (S-0130-b, S-0133-g, S-0135-d, S-0135-f, S-0136-b,
; S-0136-d, S-0139-c, S-0140-a, S-0142-j, S-0144-f, S-0144-h).
; Rule, in our words: a setter with one trump or none, unable to follow the
; bidder's trump lead or his double, throws a tile that is his only one of
; some suit, so that he is void there when the bidder's off comes. He keeps
; what he will want then: his count, his doubles and other tiles that cannot
; lose (the high tiles under doubles trump), and the last spare guarding a
; count tile of his.
; On any other throw that puts no count on the trick (he holds none, or the
; trick is neither one his partner may still take nor his partner's to give
; to), he throws a tile he need not keep, by the same list: no trump, no
; count, no double or other tile that cannot lose, not the last guard of a
; count tile (Hand 30 trick 1: the 4-0, keeping the 5-1 that guards the 4-1).
; With nothing else left but doubles and count, the guard goes (Hand 31 trick
; 3: the 5-1, the book says, for want of anything else; Hands 28 and 30,
; trick 2).
; In Hand 31 trick 4 the left setter, two trumps in hand, throws the 5-4 under
; his partner's 3-3: his one tile neither trump nor a double, and, as the book
; says, it leaves him void in fours and fives to trump them later.
; Replaces gates/c13a-shed-a-singleton.silas. How it differs: the gate fires on
; a trump lead only, and throws a lone double or the last guard of a count tile
; (the 6-0 alone among blanks but guarding the 6-4); the book keeps both
; (S-0064-c, S-0071-a: protection ranks above a void). The gate needs no trump
; held; the book's setter holds one trump or none, and does the same when the
; bidder leads a double (S-0065-c).
; The book against itself: twice its right setter throws a tile that voids
; nothing on the bidder's trump lead though a lone one was his to throw (Hand
; 28 trick 2, the 2-1 with the 6-3 alone among sixes and treys, S-0130-c;
; Hand 33 trick 5, the 1-0 with the 3-1 alone among treys). It gives no reason;
; this file follows its stated guideline, the void first (p. 48, which ranks it
; above the rest), and the other worked throws (Hands 32 and 33, trick 1).
; Re-read 2026-10-14 (#153), presuming the encoding misread: in Hand 28 the
; kept 6-3 is the second trey still out behind the 3-3, and at trick 3 it
; takes the bidder's 3-1 off for six (S-0130-c's deal as dealt); the
; candidate condition "keep a lone tile that is the top or second of its suit
; still out" explains that keep and the throws of Hands 32 and 33, trick 1
; (the 6-2 fifth among the sixes, the 6-0 last), but not Hand 33 trick 5,
; where the kept 3-1 is third and takes nothing live. The book states no
; such condition on pp. 43-49; the row stays the book against its rule, and
; the measurement that would decide it is a reason report from the right
; setter's cell at Hand 28 trick 2 (what the 6-3 is worth in his worlds).
; Against a bid of marks the book's defenders keep their pairs and throw their
; dead doubles instead (Hands 34 and 35, S-0146-d, S-0150-c: dead-double.silas
; and defend-the-84.silas); a void for a pounce is worth nothing there, and
; this rule is for points.

(include book)

(policy shed-for-a-void
  (rule throw-a-lone-tile (play lone)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (not (every-trick))
    (bidder-led led)
    (or (trump-tile led) (double led))
    (none (roles a b) (mine a) (trump-tile a) (mine b) (trump-tile b))
    (discard lone)
    (not (trump-tile lone))
    (count lone 0)
    (not (walker lone))
    (not (guards-count lone))
    (in lone suit)
    (not (trump suit))
    (none (roles other) (mine other) (in other suit) (not (tile other lone))))
  (rule throw-what-you-need-not-keep (play plain)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (not (every-trick))
    (or
      (none (roles c) (own-legal c) (count-tile c))
      (and (not (partner-may-take-it)) (not (and (last-to-play) (partner-winning)))))
    (discard plain)
    (not (trump-tile plain))
    (count plain 0)
    (not (walker plain))
    (not (guards-count plain)))
  (rule then-the-guard (play guard)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (not (every-trick))
    (or
      (none (roles c) (own-legal c) (count-tile c))
      (and (not (partner-may-take-it)) (not (and (last-to-play) (partner-winning)))))
    (discard guard)
    (not (trump-tile guard))
    (count guard 0)
    (not (walker guard))))
